  - python
abstract: >-
  Three Python scripts that reconstruct the velocity potential of a two-dimensional periodic wave tank from the shape
  of the free surface and the values of the potential on it, known at scattered points, and return the velocity field,
  in particular on the free surface. The fluid domain is meshed with Gmsh and the Laplace equation, with the potential
  imposed on the free surface, no flow through the flat bottom and periodicity in the horizontal direction, is solved by
  finite elements with the legacy FEniCS; a generator of analytic test data at random points is included.
